title: Levi Was Wrong
subtitle: The action he feared has won. What becomes of its critic?
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1921 and month >= 4 and crisis = 0 and levi_in_party = 1 and march_action = 2 and e21_central_done = 1 and e21_after_done = 0
max-visits: 1
priority: 12
on-arrival: e21_after_done = 1

= Levi Was Wrong

Paul Levi had a pamphlet half written: a reckoning with the March Action, which he was certain would end in a massacre. It did not. The pamphlet stays in his drawer.

The Left is triumphant. Ruth Fischer says in the Berlin district that the party has learned to fight, and that those who would not fight should step aside. [? if e21_march_mode = 1 : Levi's friends answer that the strike won because it was a defensive strike of the whole class, exactly what Levi always asked for. ?][? if e21_march_mode = 2 : Levi's friends answer that one lucky victory proves nothing, and that next time the Reichswehr will march. ?]

- @admit: Levi admits he was wrong, and stays.
- @warn: Levi keeps warning against adventures.
- @leave: Levi leaves the party.

@admit
subtitle: Unity, for now. The Spartacists lose their voice.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e21_levi_fate = 5;
Q.unity += 6;
Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction -= 5;
Q.offensive_satisfaction += 5;
Q.lean_unionist += 1;
Q.lean_offensive += 1;
!}

Levi writes a short article saying that he underestimated the workers of Central Germany. It is the most painful thing he has ever written. The Left reads it aloud at meetings.

@warn
subtitle: The Spartacist line. Levi stays, and the quarrel goes on.
on-arrival: e21_levi_fate = 2; luxemburgist_satisfaction += 6; offensive_satisfaction -= 8; independence += 3; lean_luxemburgist += 2

Levi publishes an article: a victory won by luck is not a method. The Left demands his expulsion. The Zentrale refers the question to the Comintern's congress.

@leave
subtitle: Levi goes, almost alone. A few friends go with him.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e21_levi_fate = 4;
Q.levi_in_party = 0;
Q.levi_split = 1;
Q.levi_advisor = 0;
for (var d of Q.districts) {
    Q['district_' + d + '_members'] *= 0.97;
}
if (Q.leading_faction == 'luxemburgist') {
    Q.leading_faction = 'unionist';
    Q.junior_faction = 'offensive';
}
Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction -= 10;
Q.offensive_satisfaction += 6;
Q.unity += 3;
!}

Levi returns his membership book with a letter to the Zentrale: the party has chosen a road he cannot follow. A few deputies and journalists go with him. The members, flushed with victory, hardly notice.
